.SHORT TERM...
Issued at 1252 PM PST Wed Nov 11 2026
(This evening through Thursday night)

The warmest day of the week is still on track for this afternoon
with a slight cool down on Thursday as the mid/upper level trough
deepens off of the West Coast. The deepening of the trough will push
the high pressure, which resulted in several days of above normal
temperatures, eastward across the Desert Southwest. Thus,
temperatures cool some 3-8 deg F on Thursday compared to this
afternoon`s maximum temperatures. In the next 24-36 hours, a cut-off
low within the larger broad troughing off of the West Coast will
develop at move toward Southern California and Baja California.
Thus, the Bay Area and north Central Coast will see little if any
impacts from this southward tracking low. Prefrontal rain is
forecast to return to return in the coastal ranges late Thursday
night into Friday morning.

Got beach plans? Check out the BEACHES section of the AFD for safety
tips and more information on the Beach Hazards Statement/High Surf
Warning and Coastal Flood Advisory.

