.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1003 AM PST Wed Nov 11 2026

VFR conditions and diurnal winds should prevail today. Moderate
confidence IFR (potentially becoming LIFR) conditions return to
Half Moon Bay, Santa Rosa, and Oakland. Low to Moderate confidence
of MVFR returning across the bay area, with low confidence (under
30%) in IFR or worse. Cloud cover is likely to increase after
09-12Z with the potential for reductions in visibility if fog is
able to develop. Fog chances are highest across the North Bay
Valleys but may impact airports along the SF Bay shoreline.
Conditions are expected to worsen through Thursday ahead of a low
pressure system arriving on Friday.

Vicinity of SFO...Fog persists along the west San Francisco Bay
shoreline, but should clear from radiation before 20z. VFR and
diurnal winds to prevail afterward. MVFR conditions come in tonight;
IFR is possible tonight, but light offshore flow may be enough to
keep it away.

SFO Bridge Approach...Some fog/low lying clouds are hanging on
between San Jose and SFO. These should clear out from radiation
before 20z. Afterwards, VFR and diurnal winds for the rest of the
day with the potential for MVFR conditions overnight.

Monterey Bay Terminals...IFR-LIFR conditions return overnight as low
cloud cover returns ahead of an incoming low pressure system.
Current thinking is that CIGs will be on the IFR-LIFR border for
MRY/SNS with clearing to occur late tomorrow morning. Otherwise,
winds remain light and onshore during the day before becoming light,
offshore overnight. Drainage winds are likely to develop at SNS
again tomorrow morning with SE winds peaking around 15 knots.

