.MARINE...
(Today through Monday)
Issued at 902 AM PST Wed Nov 11 2026

Conditions will steadily deteriorate Thursday into Friday as a
cold front approaches the coast bringing strong SW winds and
moderate rain. Gale force winds are likely during the day on
Friday with a low potential for short lived storm force gusts as
the front moves through. By Saturday, high seas will move in from
a hurricane force low moving through the NE Pacific. Significant
wave heights will reach between 25 to 30 feet on Saturday. Small
crafts will sustain heavy damage and may not survive in these
conditions.

